Subject: [ZEROX 2/4] Apply conservative performance defaults

Files modified by the generated source patch:

- io/papermc/paper/configuration/WorldConfiguration.java
- org/spigotmc/SpigotWorldConfig.java

Behavioral changes:

```diff
- public boolean doCollisionEntityLookups = true;
+ public boolean doCollisionEntityLookups = false;

- public boolean optimizeExplosions = false;
+ public boolean optimizeExplosions = true;

- public boolean updatePathfindingOnBlockUpdate = true;
+ public boolean updatePathfindingOnBlockUpdate = false;

- this.maxTntTicksPerTick = this.getInt("max-tnt-per-tick", 100);
+ this.maxTntTicksPerTick = this.getInt("max-tnt-per-tick", 16);
```

Rationale:

- Avoid repeated armor-stand collision scans where the administrator has not opted in.
- Use Paper's optimized explosion block-density calculation.
- Prevent block updates from creating large pathfinding-recalculation storms.
- Bound primed-TNT entity ticking before the dedicated explosion budget is reached.

Administrators can override generated defaults in Paper/Spigot world configuration. Redstone behavior is not changed by this patch.
